hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1261","Muhammad bin Miskin Al-Yamani narrated to us, Yahya bin Hassan narrated to us, Suleiman, who is Ibn Bilal, narrated to us, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Saad, He said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, leaning his mount, then he dismounted, prayed ten rak’ahs, and performed the Witr prayer. With one rak'ah, he prayed two rak'ahs, then he performed Witr with one rak'ah, then he prayed two rak'ahs of Fajr, then he led us in the morning prayer.” Abu Bakr said: This news clearly states that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the two rak’ahs of dawn while traveling, and the news that we narrated in the book Al-Kabir, in the sleep of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, absent from the morning prayer until the sun rose, “and that he prayed the two rak’ahs of dawn, then he prayed the morning prayer.”"
